[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-181957"] :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo create a schematic of the Cartesian product, we create a table and list the elements of the first set $A$ in a row across the top and the elements of the second set $B$ in a column down the left side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/8fe661f4daa7a5bb75dea993f46bbf8970400a798e23da4018d3e4a0b891273d.png)\n\nThen, at each intersection, we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of $A$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of $B.$\n\nOur completed $A\\times B$ schematic is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/49270545404b21e8068b35cdb59c756e1f3bc3c22608359c8d7e83389e38c7a4.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-181975/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "f50383ed-f5db-52e3-9a47-a3279815a4eb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181975/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "a41d1e81-acce-543a-84fe-97d6f5ebd73b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181975/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "43838c97-b0ad-59b9-835c-28b6c838d88c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181975/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "f8940f2e-49fb-5589-9dc6-c528426afa92" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181975/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "d126857b-cc94-59e3-b2ee-2b1f147403ba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181975/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6eef2c1-ec7a-5ddc-8ccf-069d417389ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-181975/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-181975/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-181975/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-181975/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-181975/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-181975/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181975" :question/id #uuid "e64fee60-df13-5cd7-874f-46a2aaf62710" :question/math-academy-id "q-181975" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/bf1c37a92b184cb3e6c81bbd2d653008f5eff0e3b2131f2f297a336881661c22.png)\n\nUsing the visual schematic above for the Cartesian product ${A}^{2}$ for $A={p,q,r},$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(q,q)\\in {A}^{2}$\n- $(p,r)\\in {A}^{2}$\n- ${q}^{2}\\in {A}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The set ${A}^{2}$ is equivalent to the Cartesian product $A\\times A.$\n\nThe Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo complete our schematic of $A\\times A,$ we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of the first set $(A)$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of the second set $(A)$ at each intersection.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/919ad6e16dcd1d8f02e8c15c7bd1dfa15f67232c99706dfbc1239e1f9a0f99e5.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram:\n\n- $(q,q)\\in {A}^{2}\\,✓$\n\n- $(p,r)\\in {A}^{2}\\,✓$\n\n- ${q}^{2}\\in {A}^{2}\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-181975/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b304527c-5cdc-57df-b118-e555f6f8fa5c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181975"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181978/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "478e75fb-b80e-53b7-8e4e-447dba895fe1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181978/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "1b487fd2-1d85-551b-97fc-2febb4244949" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181978/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "a23b5cde-f7f6-5d10-9e29-96160adf9dfd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181978/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "722f8484-c1fd-5fc6-9211-43dd574c1ed2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181978/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "9ca6e134-084c-54cb-89b5-c9ee8058fb29" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181978/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e4a7b22-0dec-5f23-80d6-3844ff0f3066" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answ