ate :question/answer-fields ["q-181978/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b304527c-5cdc-57df-b118-e555f6f8fa5c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181978"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181958/selection/ea272d0e1990f3adc02b42ee80de548b57b727a6fa82e1ae410ba57c0e2335ad" :answer/id #uuid "a6a529fa-e007-5d00-ae49-a9ec40768f62" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/6cceec57dbf53e768fc290d864fa770c70a6642bdc9df1309119e113241b0f34.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181958/selection/3e6203ac0b44e0ad8184a02b1fe5eb2a5ad8311609b297c471619575190f0299" :answer/id #uuid "c7de6e74-7619-5873-8fc0-65aec18be17c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/b7497f60cccce44a008c6550f356d32564c2a15e23d88f9c3764415598dc493b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181958/selection/59d05a0c48a58a42ddfb05af3dcb280427ae4eee5b9f329c9a54c1a3717f01f6" :answer/id #uuid "b9111bf8-e1f0-54c0-a265-0b1ae3a9c935" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/518415814ddb5483e4649c95e58aa41adc68ad8722279dbf99ac4c10bca206e9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181958/selection/59f0f02cb9ac140412efbbada7fb5525253dc283b1f3bce00c3f1290f7bcd7b9" :answer/id #uuid "09832da5-9400-5dba-aac3-be60d45f41cf" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/d366ec9f363cf38d84c6d741491f7e218e0bedad335f6fc1f1f954f95516f196.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181958/selection/61781f5989e4da6821959668c114ea2e5ecf109214701d43c94a53368489ff20" :answer/id #uuid "c0006f65-b3a3-540a-84a5-3489beca2575" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/a52e05a3884e5d62ffaacc73104a4f2e61fb8013fb353c850cdb974e66224a40.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181958/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "157de725-63f0-50a0-8c41-713ad037974a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-181958/selection/59d05a0c48a58a42ddfb05af3dcb280427ae4eee5b9f329c9a54c1a3717f01f6" :answer-field/choices ["q-181958/selection/ea272d0e1990f3adc02b42ee80de548b57b727a6fa82e1ae410ba57c0e2335ad" "q-181958/selection/3e6203ac0b44e0ad8184a02b1fe5eb2a5ad8311609b297c471619575190f0299" "q-181958/selection/59d05a0c48a58a42ddfb05af3dcb280427ae4eee5b9f329c9a54c1a3717f01f6" "q-181958/selection/59f0f02cb9ac140412efbbada7fb5525253dc283b1f3bce00c3f1290f7bcd7b9" "q-181958/selection/61781f5989e4da6821959668c114ea2e5ecf109214701d43c94a53368489ff20"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181958" :question/id #uuid "393bef1a-778c-53b8-a73e-75ffc95e3405" :question/math-academy-id "q-181958" :question/problem "Which of the following is a schematic of the Cartesian product $A\\times B$ for $A={p,q}$ and $B={w,z}?$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo create a schematic of the Cartesian product, we create a table and list the elements of the first set $A$ in a row across the top and the elements of the second set $B$ in a column down the left side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/6baae52e45d00d31eac732a23be655b648765c27cfcdc667c511b176d5bbbc88.png)\n\nThen, at each intersection, we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of $A$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of $B.$\n\nOur completed $A\\times B$ schematic is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/38e9d12b0c09ae066149d95235a6918712214edc147c57775da2d880b584cb9e.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-181958/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b304527c-5cdc-57df-b118-e555f6f8fa5c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181958"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-181963"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/cb3e6ef6a832f2adbbc5e096bddf2c4f6a0445fbd77a71df5617298f8dad2e51.png)\n\nBy finding the missing entries in the schematic shown above for $A\\times B,$ where $A={a,b,c}$ and $B={2,4,6},$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(4,b)\\in A\\times B$\n- $(c,6)\\in A\\times B$\n- $(a,2)\\in A\\times B$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo complete our schematic of $A\\times B,$ we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of $A$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of $B$ at each intersection.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/57d053cca53046f02201540e655030a37ba8f7a2811e7dc724cf30ca9fd3c072.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram:\n\n- $(4,b)\\notin A\\times B\\,\\times $\n\n- $(c,6)\\in A\\times B\\,✓$\n\n- $(a,2)\\in A\\times B\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-182022/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "a64cb45a-380c-594a-b48f-cf427dfc3bc4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182022/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "f213756c-e40e-5f0c-854b-0434d4ec1e2d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182022/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "65105d81-37f0-59c8-85f2-879bfc214dcf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182022/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "06801011-2bb7-51f4-ab64-a6f7a9955e8e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182022/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "63c0ce15-e25b-594a-8f39-4be2b77ba006" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182022/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdd5cca6-718d-578f-b0ba-5709bbcd077c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-182022/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-182022/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-182022/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-182022/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-182022/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-182022/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-182022" :question/id #uuid "fef8c320-85d2-5334-8cb1-417e3b026ac2" :question/math-academy-id "q-182022" :question/problem "For the sets $Z={-3,6,-9}$ and $Y=Z\\times Z,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(-3,6,-3)\\in Y$\n- $(-3,-9)\\in Y$\n- $(-9,6)\\in Y$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $Z\\times Z$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $Z$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Z.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for ${Z}^{2}=Z\\times Z$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/0c58bf1f025cc4960ce3b9dc8e1bc3bf474a521473833b27d136fd77fd6b814a.png)\n\nHence, the set $Y=Z\\times Z$ is given by\n\n$$\nY={(-3,-3),(-3,6),(-3,-9),(6,-3),(6,6),(6,-9),(-9,-3)(-9,6),(-9,-9)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-182022/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-182022"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-182011/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "a487de39-b238-5ac4-a5d8-345740c51dcb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182011/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "8bdab1ed-b5d5-50ea-b858-c3dec60ca751" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182011/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "134b9ac0-8f8f-5c45-842e-f32eda158ee9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182011/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "d3ac0495-5c45-5f29-9a3b-3db2335630cb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182011/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "07821f28-42c9-54e4-83e8-12329924de3b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/