 consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Y.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $X\\times Y$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/316a12102e4be81291f06403815cfb63749b1fd3f463c465294e031543123484.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(x,v),(x,w),(y,v),(y,w),(z,v),(z,w)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-182020/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "12ef23d3-7ce9-5c60-a2d7-8870ea55bb5f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182020/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "166b602d-1ec2-5b5c-8f1b-e160695207f9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182020/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "f03514de-d215-5c39-ac83-2c490c9d4a6e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182020/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "3ee8b030-45e0-5f4e-bcfc-699eeb8ef6e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182020/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "34e84b6d-44af-5ac3-85b7-fd72b7d7ee17" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182020/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "075dadd1-c068-5900-811f-367049667ea3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-182020/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-fiel